# Built LevelDB compendiums. Tracked deliberately (see .gitignore) so the system
# installs and runs straight from a clone, with no build step.
#
# Marking them binary stops git attempting textual diffs and 3-way merges on
# sstables — a merge of two .ldb files produces a corrupt database, not a
# conflict you can resolve by hand.
#
# NOTE this does NOT stop the working-tree churn. Foundry rewrites CURRENT and
# rotates MANIFEST-* on every world launch (LevelDB compaction), so those still
# show as modified. The real fix is a release workflow that builds packs from
# src/packs/*.yaml — see .planning/API-NOTES.md, T0.1 decision 2.
packs/** binary
packs/**/*.ldb -diff -merge
packs/**/CURRENT -diff -merge
packs/**/MANIFEST-* -diff -merge

# Source of truth for compendium content — normal text, diff these.
src/packs/**/*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
